# Mos Eisley Cantina — Tailwind exercise rules

## Scope
- Work only in `index.html`.
- Do not create CSS, JavaScript, React, components, config files, or build tooling.
- Use the Tailwind Play CDN already provided in the starter:
  `<script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>`
- Use only HTML + Tailwind utility classes.

## General implementation rules
- Follow the exercise brief exactly.
- Do not add sections, features, animations, icons, libraries, or functionality that were not requested.
- Prefer semantic HTML whenever appropriate.
- Keep the code readable and beginner-friendly.
- Do not over-engineer.
- Preserve the existing `<title>`, meta tags, CDN script, and body unless a requested Tailwind class must be added.
- Put all styling in Tailwind classes directly in the HTML.

## Page background
The `<body>` must use a dark Tatooine-inspired gradient:
- `min-h-screen`
- `text-slate-100`
- `antialiased`
- `bg-gradient-to-br`
- `from-slate-950`
- `via-violet-950/40`
- `to-amber-950/30`

## Header
Create a semantic `<header>` containing:
- `<nav aria-label="Primary">`
- Logo/badge + text `Mos Eisley Cantina`
- Navigation links:
  - Features
  - Menu
  - Live music
  - Sign in
- CTA:
  - `Reserve a booth`

Header requirements:
- Sticky on scroll using `sticky top-0`
- Semi-transparent dark background
- `backdrop-blur`
- Suitable `z-index`
- Centered max-width layout
- Comfortable horizontal and vertical padding
- Flex layout with good alignment and spacing

## Accessibility
- Every link and CTA must be keyboard focusable.
- Every interactive element must have a clearly visible `focus-visible` style.
- Prefer Tailwind utilities such as:
  - `focus-visible:outline-none`
  - `focus-visible:ring-2`
  - `focus-visible:ring-violet-400`
  - appropriate ring offset when needed
- Keep `aria-label="Primary"` on the main navigation.
- Images must have meaningful `alt` text.

## Hero
Inside `<main>`, create one hero `<section>`.

The hero section must use:
- `grid`
- `md:grid-cols-2`
- `gap-12`
- `items-center`

It must stack into one column on small screens and become two columns from the `md` breakpoint.

### Left column
Include:
1. Pill badge:
   `Open every night, 3 ABY`

2. One `<h1>`:
   `Find your watering hole on Tatooine`

3. Apply a violet-to-amber gradient only to the word `Tatooine` using:
   - `bg-gradient-to-r`
   - violet start color
   - amber end color
   - `bg-clip-text`
   - `text-transparent`

4. Add a short atmospheric paragraph related to the cantina.

5. Add two CTAs:
   - Primary violet CTA
   - Secondary outline CTA

Use appropriate spacing, readable typography, and responsive sizing.

## Hero image
Use exactly this image URL:

`https://product-builder-fullstack.s3.eu-west-3.amazonaws.com/M02_Web-Foundation/unsplash-cantina.jpeg`

Place it inside a semantic `<figure>`.

Figure requirements:
- Rounded corners
- `overflow-hidden`
- `ring-1 ring-white/10`
- Moody/dark presentation
- Responsive image using `w-full`
- Suitable object sizing
- Add a small caption strip with `<figcaption>`

## Visual direction
Use a dark sci-fi / Tatooine atmosphere:
- slate/near-black base
- violet accents
- amber accents
- subtle borders
- no bright white backgrounds

Pixel-perfect reproduction is not required.
Prioritize:
1. Correct structure
2. Correct Tailwind utilities
3. Responsive layout
4. Accessibility
5. Overall violet/amber visual direction

## Responsive behavior
At approximately 375px wide:
- Hero must be one column
- No horizontal scrolling
- Text must remain readable
- CTAs may wrap or stack naturally
- Header must remain usable without introducing a hamburger menu unless absolutely necessary

## Before finishing
Verify:
- HTML tags are correctly nested and closed
- No nested `<a>` elements
- Tailwind classes are inside `class=""`
- Header is sticky
- Hero is responsive
- `Tatooine` has gradient text
- Image URL is correct
- Every link/CTA has a visible keyboard focus state
- No extra files or technologies were added
